   v14.2 A-G variant matrix complete; B sealed as production.

   v14.4+ (2026-06-18) P3b Immediate Stop Guard:
          - SetStopLoss = MC engine-level stop, active on entry
            bar (no IOG dependency). Closes the unprotected window.
          - Distance = AbsValue((Box_Top + ATR*2.0) - Close) *
            BigPointValue. Same anchor as Frozen SL.
          - Called only when not short (MP>=0) inside consolidation
            block -> freezes when short position opens.
          - Dormant backup once custom stops tighten.

   v14.5  (2026-06-18) [TRIED + FULLY REMOVED]
          Two filters were added to address CS_BreakExit -378K leak:
            A. Strong Long Block (Daily MA gap% > 1.0 = no short entry)
            B. Fast BreakExit (15M Close > Locked_Top + 0.5 ATR)

          A/B test (4 configs MC12 same day) result:
            Config 1 v14.4 replica  : 81 trades / +238,600 / PF 1.414
            Config 2 A only         : 81 trades / +238,600 / PF 1.414
            Config 3 B only         : 85 trades / +220,600 / PF 1.372
            Config 4 v14.5 full     : 85 trades / +220,600 / PF 1.372

          Root cause of failure:
            A is a STRICT SUBSET of existing v_Macro_Block condition
              (Macro_Block already blocks when Fast > Slow; A's "gap>1%"
              is a subset). 100% redundant -> zero effect.
            B's 0.5 ATR buffer (~30-50pt) is too tight for consolidation
              noise. 27 false-trigger FastBreakExit cost -437K, only
              5 real BreakExit -98K. Combined -535K vs v14.4's -378K.
              Also shortened cooldown allowed 4 extra bad entries.

          User decision 2026-06-18: B selected = accept L4 v14.4 as
          final, stop optimizing, fully remove v14.5 code.

          See: docs/L4_v145_ab_results_20260618.md for full analysis.
          See: memory feedback_filter_redundancy_check.md for rule.

   v14.4+ (2026-06-18) P3b Immediate Stop Guard:
          - SetStopLoss = MC engine-level stop, active on entry
            bar (no IOG dependency). Closes the unprotected window.
          - Distance = AbsValue((Box_Top + ATR*2.0) - Close) *
            BigPointValue. Same anchor as Frozen SL.
          - Called only when not short (MP>=0) inside consolidation
            block -> freezes when short position opens.
          - Dormant backup once custom stops tighten.

   v14.6  (2026-07-26) INITIAL STOP HARDENING (SetStopContract + SL_Pct):

          BUG FIX - SetStopContract MISSING (same issue as L5 v19.9):
            SetStopLoss without SetStopContract = stop dollar amount
            is for the TOTAL POSITION, not per contract.
            L4 trades 2 contracts -> engine stop was 2x tighter than
            designed. 12 "Stop Loss" exits had avg distance 0.26%
            (designed ~1.5%), totaling -266,800.
            SetStopContract makes SetStopLoss PER-CONTRACT (lot-invariant).

          NEW - SL_Pct Percentage Stop Cap (SHORT mirror of L1/L3/L5):
            ATR can spike in volatile regimes, causing the ATR-based
            stop (Box_Top + ATR*2) to exceed any reasonable risk budget.
            SL_Pct caps max stop distance as pct of entry price.
            For SHORT: ceiling = EntryPrice + EntryPrice * SL_Pct / 100.
            Applied to BOTH engine stop (P3b) and custom stop (Phase 3).
            MC sweep 0-5.0 step 0.25: converge at 1.50% (SL_Pct < 1.50 degrades).
            SL_Pct = 1.50 = tightest non-degrading value (+2K net vs baseline).
            L4 SHORT wider than LONG strategies (L1=0.5%, L3=0.55%, L5=1.0%).

          v15-v16 research line CLOSED (2026-07-26):
            v15.0/v15.1/v15.1_opt/v16.0 all FAILED. L4 alpha = bear/neutral
            trap signal only. Bull market zero trades = correct behavior.
            See strategies/research/L4_v15/ and L4_v16/ for full postmortem.

   STATUS: v14.6 + SetStopContract + SL_Pct is the PRODUCTION version.
   Do NOT re-add Strong_Long_Filter or Fast_BreakExit without
   the redundancy+pass-rate analysis required by Constitution
   (memory: feedback_filter_redundancy_check.md).
